{
  "_about": "Samsung Galaxy Buds models PairFree knows. model is Samsung's model number (SM-R...), names the names the earbuds use. galaxybudsclient holds what GalaxyBudsClient's device specification gives (tools/import_galaxybudsclient.py): its name for the model and the generation it compares (newer models have higher numbers), the part of the Bluetooth name it matches (base_name), the RFCOMM service, the framing (legacy: start FE, end EE, a type and a one-byte length; standard: start FD, end DD, a two-byte length), the highest ambient sound volume step, the touch-and-hold options as [byte, option] (custom runs a phone-side action, set in Samsung's app), the colours by device id, and the features, each with the lowest state revision that has it (null: every revision). The rest is PairFree's: reports lists recordings in data/samsung/reports, notes what was found on the earbuds. samsung_app holds what Samsung's own Galaxy Buds plugin says, where PairFree has read it (com.samsung.accessory.budsunitemgr 9.0.10): the codename, the state layout, the names the plugin matches, the touch-and-hold codes and the features. It overrides galaxybudsclient field by field, and models only Samsung's plugin knows have it alone. kind is headphones for a headset.",
